{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next","id":760764,"title":"Which Supernatural Style Comes Next?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-08T10:59:39-08:00","id":760764,"title":"Which Supernatural Style Comes Next?","content":"Namely, which of the following Supernatural Merits should I make a Style Merit for next?<br /> <br /> 1. Apportation<br /> 2. Curse Effigy<br /> 3. Evil Eye<br /> 4. Hardened Exorcist<br /> 5. Incite Ecosystem<br /> 6. Laying on Hands<br /> 7. Mind of a Madman<br /> 8. Numbing Touch<br /> 9. Thief of Fate<br /> <br /> Those 9 are the Supernatural Merits where I have <i>some</i> idea of how they would expand into a style - if anyone has any other suggestions once I'm under way, I will take them into consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:34:47-08:00","id":760791,"title":"","content":"Thief of Fate seems easily expandable.<br /> <br /> Where is Incite Ecosystem from, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:42:43-08:00","id":760904,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing Poison Ivy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:55:21-08:00","id":760912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next?p=760791#post760791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thief of Fate seems easily expandable.<br /> <br /> Where is Incite Ecosystem from, though?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hurt locker, it allows someone to sic animals on people. <br /> <br /> As for the supernatural styles I'd like to see, I'd vote for Apportation, Evil Eye, Mind of a Madman, and Thief of Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:56:10-08:00","id":760913,"title":"","content":"I vote for Apportation. I really like the stuff you make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T14:00:47-08:00","id":760921,"title":"","content":"I wanna see Hardened Exorcist. I assume it is going to be only for characters without a major template, seeing as how the latter have their own powers and methods to deal with entities that must be exorcised. Mortal occultists, on the other hand, would benefit immensely from whatever advantages they can get in order to oppose entities of higher Rank. I'm guessing that the &quot;Hardened&quot; part means there will be some drawbacks related to Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:18:55-08:00","id":761217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next?p=760921#post760921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanna see Hardened Exorcist. I assume it is going to be only for characters without a major template, seeing as how the latter have their own powers and methods to deal with entities that must be exorcised. Mortal occultists, on the other hand, would benefit immensely from whatever advantages they can get in order to oppose entities of higher Rank. I'm guessing that the &quot;Hardened&quot; part means there will be some drawbacks related to Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Uhm, every single choice is based on a supernatural merit, which by definition, the vast majority of templates, major or lesser, are incapable of having. <br /> <br /> So barring dragons with that coil with the really weird name for buying supernatural merits, or someone using dark heroes in a second edition game, it pretty much mortals and stigmatics only. <br /> <br /> Sounds like you might want to look at the playtest documents <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-open-dev-dump-2/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-open-dev-dump-2/</a>.<br /> <br /> Oh that reminds me, how about a supernatural style for a microtemplate? They are just themed supernatural merits after all.<br /> <br /> Do none of them inspire you, Amechra? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T15:44:13-08:00","id":761775,"title":"","content":"Eh, the microtemplates would be a different &quot;thing&quot; - it'd be filling in, rather than expanding, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Portage (Supernatural; Style \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> You have become an expert with your &quot;trick&quot; - you can rip things through the between-spaces like no-one's business.<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Apportation \u2022\u2022\u2022, Science \u2022\u2022\u2022, Occult \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Heisenberg Uncertainty (\u2022) -</b> Due to practice with rapidly calculating vectors and rough positional coordinates, you've developed a certain deftness. Reduce any penalties you suffer to your Apportation roll by your dots in Science.<br /> <b>Tripping the Gap (\u2022\u2022) -</b> You are always a valid target for your own Apportation, regardless of whether or not you would normally be able to affect objects your size. In addition, you gain your dots in Apportation as general armor against damage inflicted by Apportation.<br /> <b>God's Own Angles (\u2022\u2022\u2022) -</b> Your mastery of inconstant positioning allows you to strike from completely unexpected angles. Whenever you spend Willpower on an attack, you may forgo the normal bonus to instead ignore up to a yard of cover between you and your target. If you spent time aiming, you may add the bonus from aiming to the number of yards of cover you can &quot;skip&quot;. If this would be sufficient to ignore the cover they are hiding behind, you also ignore any penalty from Concealment on that attack.<br /> <b>Sound of the Tindalos (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) -</b> Rather than ripping a single object through reality, you can set up a sort of &quot;standing wave&quot; around yourself, rendering your position locally undefinable. Spend one WIllpower and roll Resolve + Occult; for a number of turns equal to your Successes, you may calculate your Defense using your Resolve + Occult, and may apply your Defense against Firearms attacks and surprise attacks. In addition, your Speed increases to Size + Resolve + Science + Occult. You may snap back to reality as a Reflexive action, ending these benefits prematurely.<br /> <i>Drawback:</i> Staying unstuck from reality for too long is dangerous. You suffer 1B each turn you spend &quot;unhinged&quot; from reality. As a strange aside, you are also considered to be Infrastructure for as long as Sound of the Tindalos is active; you trigger relevant senses, have the relevant vulnerabilities, and might eventually become a Stigmatic.<br /> <b>Occult Geometries (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) -</b> Normally, there is <i>some</i> allowance for safety incorporated into Apportation - at this point, you figure out a certain level of... precision. You may now use Apportation to target specific parts of an animate character; doing so requires imposes the appropriate Called Shot penalty on top of the -3 penalty for targeting a moving part. As long as you achieve at least one success, the target character suffers one level of Aggravated damage and an appropriate tilt. As a general rule, you can use Apportation for Down and Dirty Combat once you've achieved this level of finesse.<br /> <i>Drawback:</i> For <i>obvious</i> reasons, the target of this use of Apportation is <i>always</i> considered unwilling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T18:18:31-08:00","id":761898,"title":"","content":"<i>Very</i> nice. Thank you; this should come in handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T18:34:07-08:00","id":766731,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Black Kitty-Cat [Supernatural; Style \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> You have the capacity to be a living embodiment of Murphy's Law - the best response to seeing that you are around is walking the other way.<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Thief of Fate, Manipulation \u2022\u2022, Presence \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_IKA0sXJ1o0\" target=\"_blank\">Stray Cat Strut</a> (\u2022):</b> You are an endless dynamo of good cheer and luck. You can't say that much for those who you touch. On days where you've stolen someone's luck, you gain an additional Willpower dot - this dot is filled when you first gain it, and is always spent first. Meanwhile, your victims instead <i>lose</i> one Willpower dot while suffering the effects of Thief of Fate; they immediately regain that Willpower dot once their luck returns.<br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-2CWsqGFgkA\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Kitty Rag</a> (\u2022\u2022):</b> You can intensify your luck-theft, piggybacking on deprecated elements of reality. You may spend one Willpower to let your luck-theft permeate the scene; for the rest of the scene, any character other than you that does something considered &quot;unlucky&quot; is affected by your Thief of Fate.<br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nW8S58CYQqs\" target=\"_blank\">Cat-Scratch Fever</a> (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> At least you've got your health! Again, this cannot be said about the poor people whose luck you've robbed. On any day where you've stolen someone's luck, you gain a temporary Health Level and spending Willpower to improve your Stamina gives you a +3 bonus rather than a +2 bonus. Meanwhile, your victims take 1 level of Bashing damage each time they spend Willpower while suffering the effects of Thief of Fate.<br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tat49m9Cjqo\" target=\"_blank\">Catgroove</a> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Nothing is going to ruin your groove - and everything's going to screw up theirs. On any day you've stolen someone's luck, you gain 1/1 Armor whenever you aren't wearing any other armor. Meanwhile, the poor people you stole your luck from treat applying their Defense against an attack as if it were spending Willpower for the purposes of Cat-Scratch Fever.<br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KUwjNBjqR-c\" target=\"_blank\">Cat's In The Cradle</a> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> You're a regular bad-luck charm - on any day you've stolen someone's luck, you may choose to double the benefits of either Stray-Cat Strut or Cat-Scratch Fever. If you do so, your victims lose one point of Willpower when you touch them, and take an additional level of Bashing damage due to Cat-Scratch Fever. <hr /><br /> Gee, I wonder if anyone can guess the theme to this one?<br /> <br /> This might seem a bit strong - however, most of the benefits are primarily defensive, and are mostly there to tempt you to use Thief of Fate more often. The second dot is potent, but hard to use without significant set-up.<br /> <br /> <b>The Atariya And Black Kitty-Cat</b><br /> Any character who has Luck Flows Up may substitute it for Thief of Fate for the purposes of Black Kitty-Cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 02-20-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T20:24:13-08:00","id":766788,"title":"","content":"Are there any threads or links besides this I may have missed? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'd like to see the ones you've done prior to these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T21:15:26-08:00","id":766821,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/414263-silly-silly-style-merits\">I</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/759387-supernatural-style-this-sword-here-at-my-side-don-t-act-the-way-it-should\">happen</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/733445-new-supernatural-merit-vicissitude\">to</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/512724-ghoul-families-hack\">have</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/510468-supernatural-merit-the-vampire-gene\">done</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/521440-spaaaace-tiiilts\">a</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/359205-university-as-a-setting-for-a-chronicle?p=359753#post359753\">couple</a>...<br /> <br /> I have a tendency to write merits and stuff like that instead of doing my classwork. It's... a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T15:14:46-08:00","id":770329,"title":"","content":"Wow, really loving these styles! Great companion to the merits!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Will Rotenberry</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer<br /> <b>Armory: Hurt Locker</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5031-bloodywillpower","name":"BloodyWillpower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T18:09:38-08:00","id":770423,"title":"","content":"Not that I'm industrious enough to do it myself, but I had the thought that one could make &quot;supernatural styles&quot; essentially that didn't actually use supernatural merits as the base.<br /> <br /> Why not say a vampire that can do a lot more with protean 2 than most could dream of, etc? <br /> <br /> Or if one wants to continue with the theme of making mortals more powerful, how about a style based on a skill trick from mirrors, or whatever they call the advantages for heroic mortals from SDL?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:44:39-08:00","id":772671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not say a vampire that can do a lot more with protean 2 than most could dream of, etc? </div> </div> </div>Those already exist - they're called Devotions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or if one wants to continue with the theme of making mortals more powerful, how about a style based on a skill trick from mirrors, or whatever they call the advantages for heroic mortals from SDL? </div> </div> </div>Because most of those are <i>really</i> passive? The only reason I can build more stuff off of stuff like Apportation and Thief of Fate is because they involve you <i>doing something</i>.<br /> <br /> Most Skill Tricks are either Speciality++ or something that got swallowed up by merits in 2e. The stuff in SDL... dudeness, Boosts were just &quot;you get a dot or two of [BLANK]&quot;.Yeah, you had that <i>one</i> boost that let you gain two Willpower instead of one whenever you would gain one Willpower... but that's not exactly something you can <i>build off of</i>.<br /> <hr /><br /> I might seem to be a bit hostile here, but building 5-dot styles that don't overlap (a big concern with Supernatural stuff, since they should <i>feel</i> different), which aren't lolcrazy, and which can't be easily covered by pre-existing merits is already <i>pretty challenging</i>.<br /> <br /> Having to build stuff off of glorified specialities is... not something I'd look forward to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T20:12:18-08:00","id":772754,"title":"","content":"Then don't do it. I neither made a demand or an order, and last time I checked you aren't chained up in a pit in my basement, that would be quite surprising really since I don't have a basement. <br /> <br /> I was just putting the thought out there, since adamant hand in first edition was 10 martial arts about working with the various arcana, for example, the concept has room for expansion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T21:31:28-08:00","id":772793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next?p=772754#post772754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then don't do it. I neither made a demand or an order, and last time I checked you aren't chained up in a pit in my basement, that would be quite surprising really since I don't have a basement.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just raises <i>more</i> questions! Like... where am I?<br /> <br /> I'd kinda like to go home, Mr. Man-In-Ski-Mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:14:07-08:00","id":834214,"title":"","content":"Having gotten out of the basement...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Veteran Exorcist [Supernatural; Style \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022]</b></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Hardened Exorcist</a>, Indomitable, Esoteric Armory \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Know Your Enemy (\u2022):</b> You've researched the stuff that goes bump in the night enough that you can pick out proper references in your sleep. Subtract your dots in Veteran Exorcist from the number of Successes you need to research an Ephemeral Being, to a minimum of one success. If you have access to an applicable Library, double this benefit.<br /> <b>Know Your Thoughts (\u2022\u2022):</b> You have practice determining where your thoughts end and imposed ones start. Add your dots in Veteran Exorcist to your Resolve for the purposes of any roll made to contest a Manifestation or a Condition created through a Manifestation, as well as to the number of times you must be Possessed before an Ephemeral Being may Claim you.<br /> <b>Know Your Limits (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> One of the most valuable things experience has taught you is how to recover from failure. Once per scene when you suffer a Dramatic Failure on a roll to abjure, bind, or ward against an Ephemeral Entity, you immediately gain successes equal to your dots in Veteran Exorcist towards researching that entity's Ban and Bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 02-22-2016, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:53:42-08:00","id":834239,"title":"","content":"Nice build-up on Hardened Exorcist.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> You mind if we use this for Age of Azar stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T23:18:25-08:00","id":834286,"title":"","content":"If I didn't want people to use it, I wouldn't have posted it! Just credit etc, etc.<br /> <br /> I am going to make a quick tweak - it just hit me that Hardened Exorcist <i>also</i> works for experienced spirit summoners if you let the Research bonus apply to <i>any</i> roll to research Ephemeral Beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T00:42:44-08:00","id":834313,"title":"","content":"Also...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Two Steps Ahead [Supernatural; Style \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022]</b></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mind of a Madman, Eye For The Strange<br /> <b>The Red String Web (\u2022):</b> You may treat the involvement of anyone you are tracking with Mind of a Madman in a crime scene as supernatural for the purposes of Eye For The Strange. On an Exceptional Success, the ST should reveal some detail of the culprit's world-view rather than a piece of folklore.<br /> <b>Cold Hard Hunches (\u2022\u2022):</b> It's hard to hide from someone who knows you inside out. Reduce any total penalties you suffer when investigating and tracking the culprit due to the Alternate Identity or Anonymous merits, or any similar penalties, by your dots in Two Steps Ahead.<br /> <b>A Bit Too Similar (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> You find yourself slipping into a similar mindset to the culprit. You gain one of their personal Breaking Points while in their mindset, and gain a basic run-down of <i>why</i> it is a Breaking Point. In addition, you are aware of whenever you would fulfil the culprit's Vice.<br /> <b>Key Under The Doormat (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> You know what their passwords are, where they store the keys, and when they bought the milk; oh, and they're out of toilet paper. Whenever you encounter a password or lock set up by or belonging to the culprit, you may spend one Willpower as an Instant action to bypass it with minimum fuss.<br /> <b>Utterly Predictable (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> When you know how someone thinks, it becomes incredibly hard for them to pin you down. You apply your Defense against surprise attacks and firearms attacks made by the culprit, and ignore any bonuses they would get from aiming at you.<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> It could have been crazier - the original name was PreCrime Division, and involved finding culprits for crimes that <i>hadn't happened yet</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T04:48:32-08:00","id":834368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next?p=834313#post834313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could have been crazier - the original name was PreCrime Division, and involved finding culprits for crimes that <i>hadn't happened yet</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone's a Minority Report fan.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Still, I can see that concept being folded into a Precognition Merit, if ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T05:13:19-08:00","id":834376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next?p=834368#post834368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone's a Minority Report fan.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Still, I can see that concept being folded into a Precognition Merit, if ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Philip K. Dick <i>in general</i>. And yeah, it would be more of a precognition thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:36:19-08:00","id":834665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next?p=834286#post834286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I didn't want people to use it, I wouldn't have posted it! Just credit etc, etc.<br /> <br /> I am going to make a quick tweak - it just hit me that Hardened Exorcist <i>also</i> works for experienced spirit summoners if you let the Research bonus apply to <i>any</i> roll to research Ephemeral Beings.</div> </div> </div> </div> That could be very useful. To starve and exorcise spirit A, you summon spirit B, which has a purview that clashes with that of A. If the exorcist is smart, spirit B will have weaknesses that are more easily exploited than those of A, so there won't be an endless cycle of solutions turning into problems.<br /> <br /> I loved all the Styles in this thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-21-2016, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:42:01-08:00","id":834673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next?p=834665#post834665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That could be very useful. To starve and exorcise spirit A, you summon spirit B, which has a purview that clashes with that of A. If the exorcist is smart, spirit B will have weaknesses that are more easily exploited than those of A, so there won't be an endless cycle of solutions turning into problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a line that came up in a Let's Play during an incidental conversation about X-Men which I think nicely sums up one of the most commonly available semipalatable solutions to major supernatural problems in the Chronicles of Darkness:<br /> <br /> &quot;That's one of my favorite fictional concepts, like, 'We have <u>solved</u> the problem \u2014 in a way that has caused us a new problem that is <u>not as bad</u>, but will <u>never go away ever</u>.'&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T00:45:43-07:00","id":1131153,"title":"","content":"So. I was going to post some Styles, wasn't I?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Antenna Mind [Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Technopathy \u2022\u2022, Intelligence \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b><i>Delete (\u2022):</i></b> You may choose to make your Technopathy destructive - whenever you use Technopathy, you may choose to assign an additional success to a parameter. If you do, any information you learn regarding that parameter can no longer be uncovered through mundane means - logs are wiped, signals become untraceable, and media is garbled.<br /> <i>Drawback</i>: Unfortunately, using your Technopathy this way is even more stressful on the poor technology you are accessing - treat it as an additional usage for the purposes of shorting out devices or garbling the signal.<br /> <b><i>Move (\u2022\u2022):</i></b> Your memories are just media - as a result, you can store them. Whenever you successfully recall details of one of your memories, you may reflexively spend one Willpower to store it in a piece of storage medium that's within range of your Technopathy.<br /> <b><i>Edit (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</i></b> You can use your brain as a full editing suite - whenever you use Delete on a piece of information, you may instead replace the obscured information with a falsified version of your own design. Any attempts to determine that the replaced information is fake suffers your dots in Antenna Mind as a penalty.<br /> <b><i>Broadcast (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</i></b> You are a walking, talking hotspot, with your spine acting as an organic antenna. You may use Technopathy on any device within a number of yards equal to your Intelligence + Occult - in addition, you may selectively broadcast your thoughts to electronics within this range, mixing in fragments of sounds and visuals from your subconscious to create a coherent &quot;program&quot;.<br /> <b><i>Effortless (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</i></b> Concentrating to filter out the signals is no longer necessary - the signals picked up by your technopathy are no more distracting than the conversation at a quiet cocktail party. Technopathy and Move no longer require you to spend Willpower - they are as natural to you as breathing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Regent of Beasts [Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Animal Possession \u2022\u2022, Incite Ecosystem \u2022<br /> <b><i>Crown of Claws (\u2022)</i>:</b> You may add your dots in Regent of Beasts to your dice pools for Animal Possession and Incite Ecosystem. If you score an Exceptional Success on rolls to use those supernatural merits, you may have their effects last until the next sunrise rather than a single scene.<br /> <b><i>A Snarled Command (\u2022\u2022):</i></b> You may perform Social Maneuvering with animals, using Animal Ken as the most appropriate skill. More importantly, you have a Perfect impression with any animal under the effects of Incite Ecosystem - at least, for the purposes of immediate, purely physical orders.<br /> <b><i>The Queen Surveys Her Court (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</i></b> You gain the Bonded condition - rather than applying to a single animal, it applies to any creature you have aggravated with Incite Ecosystem. Additionally, you may reflexively spend one Willpower while possessing an animal to mentally &quot;leap&quot; to another applicable animal that you can see.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}